<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">1 November in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">7 events that happened on 1 November, from 1512 to 1993.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1512 CE <span class="tih-ago">514 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Michelangelo's Sistine Chapel ceiling is shown to the public</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">After four years of work, Michelangelo's ceiling frescoes in the Sistine Chapel were unveiled for the feast of All Saints. Its scenes from Genesis, including the Creation of Adam, became a pinnacle of Renaissance art.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/renaissance">Renaissance</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1604 CE <span class="tih-ago">422 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Othello is performed before James I at Whitehall</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The King's Men performed Shakespeare's Othello in the Banqueting House at Whitehall, the earliest recorded performance of the play. Its tragedy of jealousy and manipulation remains among his most performed works.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/lisbon" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/lisbon.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1755 CE <span class="tih-ago">271 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">An earthquake and tsunami destroy Lisbon</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">On All Saints' Day a massive earthquake, followed by a tsunami and fires, destroyed most of Lisbon and killed tens of thousands. The catastrophe stirred Enlightenment debates on providence and spurred early seismology.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lisbon">Lisbon</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1800 CE <span class="tih-ago">226 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">John Adams becomes the first president to live in the White House</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">John Adams moved into the unfinished President's House in Washington. The next day he wrote to his wife Abigail: 'May none but honest and wise men ever rule under this roof.'</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1848 CE <span class="tih-ago">178 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The first medical school for women opens in Boston</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Samuel Gregory opened the Boston Female Medical School, later the New England Female Medical College, with twelve students. It was the first institution founded to train women in medicine.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/england">England</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/boston">Boston</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1914 CE <span class="tih-ago">112 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Von Spee's squadron defeats the Royal Navy at Coronel</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Off the coast of Chile, Admiral Maximilian von Spee's German East Asia Squadron sank two British cruisers, killing Rear-Admiral Cradock and some 1,600 men. It was Britain's first naval defeat in a century.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/british-empire">British Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/royal-navy">Royal Navy</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1993 CE <span class="tih-ago">33 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">The Maastricht Treaty creates the European Union</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The Treaty on European Union came into force, establishing the EU alongside the European Communities. It introduced EU citizenship and set the path to economic and monetary union and the euro.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/european-union">European Union</a></div></div></li></ol>
